WEBVTT

00:01:28.209 --> 00:01:31.546
as we look at national inaction too often,

00:01:31.587 --> 00:01:35.258
there'll be many people wondering
how we're going to take this challenge on.

00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:38.261
And even if we're going to be successful.

00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:39.887
And I understand it,

00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:42.682
so many people around the world
will be losing hope.

00:01:43.432 --> 00:01:47.770
But my message today is there is hope,
and it’s hiding in plain sight.

00:01:47.812 --> 00:01:50.773
And I believe there's huge
hope in our cities.

00:01:51.357 --> 00:01:53.442
So consider these four numbers.

00:01:53.818 --> 00:01:55.111
Three,

00:01:55.153 --> 00:01:56.529
55,

00:01:56.571 --> 00:01:58.072
75,

00:01:58.114 --> 00:01:59.490
80.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:03.995
Cities occupy less than three percent
of the Earth's land surface.